          {
            "@value": "The C.O.M. Luxia II Gold is a rare and exquisite 35mm half-format miniature camera manufactured in 1952 by the Italian company Costruzioni Ottico Meccaniche Italiane (C.O.M.I.) in Rome. It is characterised by its gold-plated metal casing with brown reptile leather, which gives it a luxurious and eye-catching appearance.",
